The English advising office noticed that you received an Academic Status Report for at least one of your [spring A session] classes. Academic Status Reports are notifications from the professor that there are potential issues with your grade in the class. It is important to follow up quickly to ensure that you complete the course successfully. 
Here are some next steps to consider: 
-	Speak with your professor to determine why the Academic Status Report was given and what you can do to improve your grade
-	Seek tutoring to discuss academic strategies to be more successful in your class: https://students.asu.edu/academic-success
-	If you feel you will not be able to pass the class at this point, you might consider withdrawing from the class by the course withdrawal deadline, which is [this Friday, January 29th] 
Academic advisors are here for you if you have any questions or need any help at all. Please feel free to schedule an advising appointment any time if you would like assistance: https://english.clas.asu.edu/advising. 

